{
  "name": "CheapClankers - model access check and one capped chat",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5933b61d-4368-46c6-a8b8-56dbdd8785ec",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "bf0c065f-fc57-4fb8-8a54-d6dd0dac2770",
      "name": "Configure request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "base",
              "name": "baseUrl",
              "value": "https://api.cheapclankers.com/v1",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "model",
              "name": "model",
              "value": "REPLACE_WITH_ENABLED_CHAT_MODEL_ID",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b7240ca1-583f-4623-8732-3911f0c97bc9",
      "name": "List accessible models",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $('Configure request').first().json.baseUrl + '/models' }}",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a6349f66-4778-4916-8998-81f60e23465f",
      "name": "Selected model accessible?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        720,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "access",
              "leftValue": "={{ Array.isArray($json.data) && $json.data.some(model => model.id === $('Configure request').first().json.model) }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0c7429b6-065c-49f1-a4a7-93145b8b8151",
      "name": "Send one capped chat",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        960,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Configure request').first().json.baseUrl + '/chat/completions' }}",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ { model: $('Configure request').first().json.model, messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Say hello in one short sentence.' }], max_tokens: 128, stream: false } }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e257cf4e-2bc0-4c07-a994-0b4e02b55259",
      "name": "Stop: model absent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stopAndError",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        960,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "errorMessage": "The selected model was not returned for this key. Check the exact model ID and permissions. No completion was sent."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b7d3531a-ae89-4f0a-8933-976ba6bdc3f4",
      "name": "Setup and limits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -550,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThis manual workflow helps developers diagnose a custom AI API setup before inference. It lists models accessible to your key, checks an exact selected ID, and sends one chat-completions request only when that ID appears. A missing model stops execution without a chat request. Success returns the response JSON, including `choices[0].message.content`. HTTP errors stop execution; automatic retries are off. A listed model establishes access, not current availability or chat support.\n\n### Setup\nCreate a CheapClankers account and server-side API key. In n8n, create a Header Auth credential with name `Authorization` and value `Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`. Select it on BOTH HTTP nodes. Never paste a real key into this workflow export. In Configure request, replace the model placeholder with an enabled chat-capable ID from the [catalogue](https://cheapclankers.com/models). Keep the production API root unless testing a trusted fixture.\n\n### Customization\nThe example sends a short greeting with a 128-token output cap and 30-second timeout. Real requests consume prepaid USD credit; review usage before retrying interruptions. Each manual run can send another paid request. Saved executions are disabled here. Tested with n8n 2.48.5 against isolated fixtures, not live inference. [API setup](https://cheapclankers.com/docs). Maintained by CheapClankers.",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "65799d0e-1613-407a-98a4-ddb6e1fd8f54",
      "name": "Access check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        190,
        -240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Check access before inference\nSet an exact chat model ID, list accessible models, and branch on whether that ID appears. Missing models stop before a paid request.",
        "height": 470,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9c6ffb5f-7a88-4ad2-a932-7960f98611ad",
      "name": "One request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        940,
        -240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send once or stop\nThe success branch sends one capped chat. The false branch explains missing access. HTTP failures stop; check credit, protocol and availability before retrying.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
  ],
